All five findings fixed, each pinned by a test that was watched failing without it.

**BLOCKER 1** — `Statement::Import` now declares the module's `set`/`constant` names into the scope it is written in (`src/analyzer.rs:308`), read out of the module file by the new `vm::module_bound_names` (`src/vm.rs:224`). Every test in `tests/constant_test.rs` now runs the real pipeline through the new `redblue::run_source_value` (`src/lib.rs:69`) instead of `run_isolated`, which skipped the analyzer.

**BLOCKER 2** — `analyzer` collects constant- and import-bound names before the walk and consults them only inside a body that runs at a call (`deferred_depth`/`bound_later`, `src/analyzer.rs:110`). A top-level read before the declaration is still the unknown variable it was, so no gate was widened.

**BLOCKER 3** — `Opcode::DeclareConst` (`DECLARE_CONST`, byte 46) with `FORMAT_VERSION` 2 → 3; `docs/BYTECODE.md` updated with the instruction row, the version row and the compiled form.

**MAJOR 4/5** — a module's `set` (and the name an import binds) goes through `Vm::bind_module_name`/`refuse_constant_rebind`, shared with `set_var`; `Vm::modules` makes a re-import a no-op.

Moving the tests onto the real pipeline also exposed a sixth defect (FINDINGS §8): the analyzer declared every `set` in the scope it was written in while the VM binds a new name globally, so `rb run` refused programs the interpreter runs. `declare_assigned`/`declare_constant` now mirror `set_var`/`bind_constant`.

Gates: `cargo fmt --all -- --check` pass · `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` pass · `cargo test --all-targets` 460 passed, 0 failed, 0 ignored · `cargo test --doc` 1 passed. `./rbops/verify.sh` still cannot run (no `rbops/` in this checkout) — recorded as not run, not as passed.
